# Thin Shell — Package Operator naming inventory

Phase **4bx** locks the honesty claim: **shell is Operator-named**; package surfaces may keep product `Denali*` identifiers until Architect scopes rename waves.

## Verdict

| Layer | Naming | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `apps/web` hand-written (`src/`, `app/`) | Operator / product-blind | **Clean** — no `Denali*` symbols; no static `@app-cloud/workspace-denali` imports outside generated bootstrap |
| Generated §2.4 loaders / themes / i18n | Opaque package paths | **Intentional** — not a naming defect |
| `packages/workspaces/denali` | Product namespace `Denali*` | **Accepted** — ~310 export decls; rename is polish, not thin-shell DoD |

## Why not big-bang rename

1. Shell already consumes package UI via Pattern B registries + Operator facades.
2. Renaming ~310 exports touches UI, wizard, HTTP, finance, tests, and package `exports` map — high churn / low architectural leverage.
3. Product tokens inside a product package are allowed; the thin-shell rule forbids them in the **host**.

## Inventory (as-built snapshot)

Approximate `export … Denali*` declarations under `packages/workspaces/denali/src` (Phase 4bx count):

| Area | ~Count |
| --- | --- |
| `ui/` | ~151 |
| `http/` | ~23 |
| `rules/` / `wizard/` / `field-registry/` / … | remaining → **~310 total** |

Exact counts drift; arch tests lock the **shell-clean** rule, not the package count.

## Optional rename waves (Architect YES only)

| Wave | Scope | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| W1 | Chrome/view surfaces already mirrored as Operator in shell | Alias `Operator*` = `Denali*` then delete Denali export after consumers migrate |
| W2 | Pure helpers dual-published on capabilities | Prefer capability symbols; keep package helpers private |
| W3 | Deep UI widgets | Rename only when editing those files anyway |

**Forbidden:** renaming package symbols to chase hostile score; introducing shell `Denali*` imports during rename.

